#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-AD0709 expect=noViolation domain=ADSL
#note "The ONLY pin of the wildcard-index carve-out on an UNPROTECTED carrier. CDISC-AD0709 (like CDISC-AD0018) lacks PMDA-AD0018's leading varname() == var_name(\"LIBRARY\") conjunct, so the exclusion leaf is the one thing standing between a template-named column and a finding. CRITy carries a Library label ('Analysis Criterion y') and a differing dataset label ('Wrong Label'), so every other conjunct is satisfied; the shipped leaf varname() !~ /[a-z]/ - the engine's own WildcardExpander template predicate - recognises the lower-case marker and keeps the rule silent. AGE is the positive control in the same dataset: an ordinary upper-case name whose labels agree, silent for the ordinary reason. Pins Fix #282 (ruling M2-D15). The previous leaf /(?:^|[^A-Z])(?:y|zz|xx|w)(?:[^A-Z]|$)/ needed the marker to follow a non-upper-case character and matched 0 of 143 real ADaM template names, so CRITy would have fired here."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
#library variable-metadata ADSL AGE label="Age" simpleDatatype=Num
#library variable-metadata ADSL CRITy label="Analysis Criterion y"
#expectViolationCount 0
dataset ADSL
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col AGE type=Num label="Age"
col CRITy type=Char label="Wrong Label"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | 56 | AGE-GT-60
---
